CLI-06  option array with every entry set to -1 (METIS' "use the default" marker)
  ./cli06 kway | rec | nodend      (0-based 40x40 grid, options[0..39] = -1)
  ./cli06 num2                     (NUMBERING = 2 with 0-based arrays: must be rejected)
Note: libmetis treats an entry equal to -1 as "default". The real METIS_SetDefaultOptions() starts from -1 but then sets
NUMBERING to 0 (stated from memory, not checked against the METIS sources here), so only callers that fill or memset the
whole array with -1 themselves reach this; Scotch's own METIS_SetDefaultOptions() zero-fills.
Pristine 7.0.17 and 7.0.18 (32-bit and 64-bit; 7.0.18 re-run by the independent reviewer, 20 s timeout, rc=124 for all three):
  kway:   never returns (killed by timeout 20 s)
  rec:    never returns (killed by timeout 20 s). On 7.0.17 it crashed on the NULL ubvec (CLI-02); CLI-02 is fixed in 7.0.18,
          so on 7.0.18 it hangs like kway.
  nodend: never returns
  num2:   AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow ... kgraph_map_ml.c  (Scotch builds a base-2 graph from 0-based arrays)
patched (0004): kway: ret=1 objval=80 part[0]=1 | rec: ret=1 objval=80 | nodend: ret=1 | num2: ERROR: _SCOTCH_METIS_V5_PartGraph: invalid numbering option, ret=-2
